cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use acspeed or its published results, please cite it as below."
title: "acspeed: a cloud-agnostic benchmark for agent-cloud operation efficiency"
abstract: >-
  acspeed benchmarks how fast a cloud is to operate when an AI coding agent is driving it. A headless
  agent is given a real application, a real cloud account and a task; the run is timed end to end and
  the elapsed wall-clock is split into the part the cloud spent, the part the agent spent, and a
  remainder held by neither. The repository contains the harness, the task suite, and 94 published
  runs across AWS, GCP and Azure with the redacted agent transcript behind every reported number.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zivanovic"
    given-names: "Milos"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/milosz94/agent-cloud-speed"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - cloud computing
  - LLM agents
  - reproducibility
  - performance measurement
